{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Net Present Value.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Net Present Value.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"net present value net present value","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Net Present Value.md","fileName":"Net Present Value.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Net Present Value","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 22:42\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Big Data Project Value Management]] [[Cloud Business Value and Finance]] [[Energy Systems Appraisal]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Big Data Project Value Management","Cloud Business Value and Finance","Energy Systems Appraisal","Internal Rate of Return","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Net Present Value.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Net Present Value.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"net present value net present value","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Net Present Value.md","fileName":"Net Present Value.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Net Present Value","heading":"Net Present Value","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Net present value sums future cash inflows and outflows after discounting them to a common present time. A positive value indicates that expected discounted benefits exceed costs under the chosen rate.\n\nFor interdependent subprojects, changing the running order changes the dates of costs and benefits and can therefore change the portfolio's value.\n\nNPV can compare a stream of recurring cloud-service payments with the up-front cost of owned infrastructure by expressing both at the same present time. It can also convert a capital amount into an equivalent recurring stream. A positive NPV indicates that discounted benefits exceed the initial and continuing costs under the chosen discount rate.\n\nFor an energy-technology investment, the same calculation places equipment cost, future fuel savings, operation and maintenance, and eventual residual value on one present-value basis. Different payment timing can change which technical alternative is economically preferable. [[Internal Rate of Return]] is the discount rate at which this NPV becomes zero, so it gives a related test against the cost of capital.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Big Data Project Value Management","Cloud Business Value and Finance","Energy Systems Appraisal","Internal Rate of Return","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Net Present Value.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Net Present Value.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"net present value net present value","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Net Present Value.md","fileName":"Net Present Value.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Net Present Value","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf]]\n\n[[cloudcomputing_mit.epub]]\n[[directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Big Data Project Value Management","Cloud Business Value and Finance","Energy Systems Appraisal","Internal Rate of Return","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}